    q: 'Is core electrical engineering a good field for women in India?',
    a: 'Yes, and hiring is actively improving, not just symbolically. PSUs, DISCOMs, and large private manufacturers such as Siemens, ABB, and Schneider Electric run specific diversity-hiring pushes for electrical and power-sector roles, and site-heavy EPC or substation work increasingly offers structured safety and support policies rather than assuming it is unsuitable by default. The practical filter is the same as for any candidate: build one visible proof project and target companies with a genuine track record on inclusion in the specific sub-field, power systems, renewables, or VLSI, rather than ruling out site-based roles on assumption alone.',
